-- Probe fixture for the string-ordering runtime builtin (__l4_str_cmp).
--
-- jl4-service (the REFERENCE) evaluates STRING GREATER THAN via
-- Data.Text's Ord. This fixture pins the observable ordering semantics
-- so the differential parity gate — not just unit tests — catches any
-- code-point-vs-code-unit divergence in the WASM runtime's __l4_str_cmp.
--
-- The curated cases in str-ordering-probe.cases.json include the astral
-- vs high-BMP trap: "😀" (U+1F600) vs "". JavaScript's native `<`
-- compares UTF-16 code UNITS (😀 -> 0xD83D 0xDE00, whose high surrogate
-- 0xD83D < 0xE000) and would answer FALSE; Unicode code-POINT order
-- (U+1F600 > U+E000) answers TRUE. __l4_str_cmp must match whatever the
-- reference does.

@export gt
GIVEN a IS A STRING
      b IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE gt IF a GREATER THAN b

@export ge
GIVEN a IS A STRING
      b IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE ge IF a AT LEAST b

@export lt
GIVEN a IS A STRING
      b IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE lt IF a LESS THAN b

@export le
GIVEN a IS A STRING
      b IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE le IF a AT MOST b
